#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115067 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a69f2883-64f8-51a6-9771-d5a885809ef6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Blocks in Partitioned Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "e4bfb0c6-dff9-501b-9507-6b5c2299fb55" :question/math-academy-id "e-9093" :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- $M_{11},$ which is a $1 \\times 2$ block\n\n- $M_{12},$ which is a $1 \\times 3$ block\n\n- $M_{21},$ which is a $2 \\times 2$ block\n\nFind the dimensions of the block $M_{22}$." :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/2ebec2a87fd922bcbe30ee648e102188b48854abcad34d88cc18695cac67e1bd.png)\n\nTherefore,  $M_{22}$ must be a $2 \\times 3$ block."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115068 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "6fe1d3e1-27a7-5e9d-9776-d66c19dae753" :question/math-academy-id "e-9094" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/a610512000d95e3ed80559431e25501a9d498d342e7c180864720bbeb2ee10d4.png)" :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/f6e977aff21319bb8e0cbb251d36577966f84060e809e3485f9019e85cd3538e.png)\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/597e27b2f470bc60717eb3341d2f3e87f411c0a4c796a58ee3aa83c691971517.png)\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115069 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b507561-8134-50ff-8c23-c4ecc546450d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Determinant of a Block Diagonal or Block Triangular Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e0360a5e-97c7-5a9b-9d13-ba05360e4d78" :question/math-academy-id "e-9096" :question/problem "Find \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/f9f02df9d1e971ccea2d5abb67f95866bb334e636e5d39ec59d14a617d8f15f0.png)\ngiven that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041065/assets/58f57ca9a1782c7edc2367b2aed9798e8e2c1eb8318000e6202b3fa0746c6a90.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have  a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the determinants of the diagonal blocks:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & e & 4 \\\\ 0 & h & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}e & 4 \\\\ h & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "150adcfa-c257-57d2-b5aa-60b2b722ebb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315690} {:answer/id #uuid "58fcb4dc-c24a-5e70-802d-784912444ee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315691} {:answer/id #uuid "abcef4c7-98ae-518a-9145-ae835e7b6c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315692} {:answer/id #uuid "18190dd9-3eb5-52c6-8f33-ee287ea975c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315693} {:answer/id #uuid "b100936c-f216-5a27-9755-1139ca23ee8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b100936c-f216-5a27-9755-1139ca23ee8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315694} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ccfc720-7cde-5838-b866-ad7d7b97f187" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c07f2a41-0b84-51be-b671-ed8827d6cdfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109247" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b507561-8134-50ff-8c23-c4ecc546450d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Determinant of a Block Diagonal or Block Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd3e51d6-6d43-54c2-abd1-9ac4d52ea628" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315697} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b21485-912b-5118-b9d5-f560e002558a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315698} {:answer/id #uuid "bf4fb0b5-ad2d-5083-8e69-accc693881b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315699} {:answer/id #uuid "0604da83-168d-5868-b7ce-e218590d7141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315700} {:answer/id #uuid "0b4993ac-c29e-5063-b465-032cc20a8d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b4993ac-c29e-5063-b465-032cc20a8d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315701} :answer-field/id #uuid "8611c250-fdce-5d6d-a70e-858665ef0758" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7dc5732a-1ec2-518d-b117-eb2600bb1b85" :question/math-academy-id "q-109266" :question/problem "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & x & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}x & -1 \\\\ 5 & y\\end{aligned}|=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & x & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & x & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}x & -1 \\\\ 5 & y\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-90.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b507561-8134-50ff-8c23-c4ecc546450d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Determinant of a Block Diagonal or Block Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f1b458c-5237-5ac8-b3aa-d819e8d20541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315704} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3d2ca9-9333-510e-91bb-d2be35ae84e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315705} {:answer/id #uuid "78f81c67-a31b-5726-b794-8b31f1113093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315706} {:answer/id #uuid "8b71e710-d579-5003-a825-48f18d2bd780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315707} {:answer/id #uuid "bfba3269-624b-55e6-8896-a8c0b88525b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78f81c67-a31b-5726-b794-8b31f1113093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315706} :answer-field/id #uuid "762aa0a5-9485-5781-972d-86bfab080831" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48d26bc3-1264-5e8a-96c1-206a84a69b6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-109267" :question/problem "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}v & w & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}v & w \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a block diagonal matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}v & w & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}v & w & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & w \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a69f2883-64f8-51a6-9771-d5a885809ef6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Blocks in Partitioned Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1055faad-005f-5767-bb2d-c8e5cf6bbfa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315711} {:answer/id #uuid "9d17f096-2843-5a91-ac27-bfb626719737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315712} {:answer/id #uuid "88f7e19b-ee3f-5055-8ab0-0ce1d2c9d8cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315713} {:answer/id #uuid "8fae12a6-47dd-5522-b27a-0a90d41e887c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315714} {:answer/id #uuid "88978316-3f90-599c-8902-d6c11255d403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d17f096-2843-5a91-ac27-bfb626719737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315712} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c4faa1-5572-5cff-adf0-cd2214f1b7a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90463106-e9a7-506c-adb4-c9f4e944b380" :question/math-academy-id "q-131332" :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- ${M}_{12},$ which is a $2\\times 4$ block\n\n- ${M}_{21},$ which is a $3\\times 1$ block\n\n- ${M}_{22},$ which is a $3\\times 4$ block\n\nWhat are the dimensions of ${M}_{11}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}?\\times ? & 2\\times 4 \\\\ 3\\times 1 & 3\\times 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${M}_{11}$ must be a $2\\times 1$ block."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a69f2883-64f8-51a6-9771-d5a885809ef6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Blocks in Partitioned Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e8e75b0-ad1d-54f4-9ec3-97009a7a91b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315718} {:answer/id #uuid "9e9c0707-1e4c-5c08-b1e4-f11263a16f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315719} {:answer/id #uuid "da8fffbc-714a-5f32-a223-a935adb00295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315720} {:answer/id #uuid "13437dcb-987a-5406-ac1a-8c1d5bbcd444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315721} {:answer/id #uuid "a001392f-fdb0-58b3-af5a-b54d4945bdca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e8e75b0-ad1d-54f4-9ec3-97009a7a91b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315718} :answer-field/id #uuid "d668e9ad-aa29-5f13-beca-1b592da57585" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f3f4c50-019c-51d3-809e-e937b1944b13" :question/math-academy-id "q-131333" :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- ${M}_{11},$ which is a $3\\times 3$ block\n\n- ${M}_{12},$ which is a $3\\times 2$ block\n\n- ${M}_{21},$ which is a $2\\times 3$ block\n\nWhat are the dimensions of ${M}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3\\times 3 & 3\\times 2 \\\\ 2\\times 3 & ?\\times ?\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${M}_{22}$ must be a $2\\times 2$ block."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b507561-8134-50ff-8c23-c4ecc546450d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Determinant of a Block Diagonal or Block Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1683765-85cf-553b-a257-fec436aa66de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315725} {:answer/id #uuid "2e65d65b-b30e-5c3e-b304-cafe1cc8efe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315726} {:answer/id #uuid "25210cef-1df5-50b8-bb75-f3fddb7253e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315727} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1e8579-670f-5dc3-bd65-3c0b0aac7125" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315728} {:answer/id #uuid "27875b50-84c0-5f0b-8344-a6001697ec4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25210cef-1df5-50b8-bb75-f3fddb7253e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315727} :answer-field/id #uuid "e78289fb-a066-5ef3-b87b-80d68538761a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d4543cb-b0a6-54a1-a9b2-aa6b974ff683" :question/math-academy-id "q-131675" :question/problem "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}v & 5{w}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3v & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 5\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}v & 5{w}^{2} \\\\ 3v & 2\\end{aligned}|=\\frac{1}{7}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a block diagonal matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}v & 5{w}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3v & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}v & 5{w}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3v & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & 5{w}^{2} \\\\ 3v & 2\\end{aligned}|\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a69f2883-64f8-51a6-9771-d5a885809ef6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Blocks in Partitioned Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0686d40-ea5e-5844-9cbc-75347d608403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315731} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a84043-814a-5b34-97f8-ceaee5822e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315732} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3e0095-0560-5a6f-af3a-4addeeafc02d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315733} {:answer/id #uuid "e5fef67b-1240-5bdb-93f0-5eeeebac828d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315734} {:answer/id #uuid "6db5d148-072b-5e4c-b47c-40982e7af415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0686d40-ea5e-5844-9cbc-75347d608403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315731} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6238265-aef2-592b-acc1-37e22154d313" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adbfea45-b5a1-50e3-b354-7bc863f46572" :question/math-academy-id "q-32130" :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- ${M}_{11},$ which is a $3\\times 2$ block\n\n- ${M}_{12},$ which is a $3\\times 1$ block\n\n- ${M}_{22},$ which is a $2\\times 1$ block\n\nWhat are the dimensions of the block ${M}_{21}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3\\times 2 & 3\\times 1 \\\\ ?\\,\\times \\,? & 2\\times 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${M}_{21}$ is a $2\\times 2$ block."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a69f2883-64f8-51a6-9771-d5a885809ef6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Blocks in Partitioned Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d189e08e-bf14-5a15-bbb4-836037f9527f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315738} {:answer/id #uuid "5654e5a9-0d9a-5e4d-90de-74e47694b8dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315739} {:answer/id #uuid "c0011917-2033-5de5-a1a5-3f0e349bb5d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315740} {:answer/id #uuid "4d629142-2866-5c14-8ae8-afd107317dfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315741} {:answer/id #uuid "3535463a-b41d-564d-8ded-d8b4344e4902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d189e08e-bf14-5a15-bbb4-836037f9527f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315738} :answer-field/id #uuid "b57331b5-edd6-584f-b58d-b1f381406cef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9eca7e02-b0cd-5cc2-a45f-366c088ecac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-32173" :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- ${M}_{12},$ which is a $2\\times 1$ block\n\n- ${M}_{21},$ which is a $2\\times 3$ block\n\n- ${M}_{22},$ which is a $2\\times 1$ block\n\nWhat are the dimensions of ${M}_{11}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}?\\times ? & 2\\times 1 \\\\ 2\\times 3 & 2\\times 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${M}_{11}$ must be a $2\\times 3$ block."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f27f7f-3a66-5e1c-9e28-510f9f15421d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315745} {:answer/id #uuid "fee8d530-baf5-5470-b734-df79eb26de9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315746} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7bebe3-2cee-5d05-949e-91f9a22cfb65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315747} {:answer/id #uuid "96002967-ff07-5fe6-945f-158c3810a07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315748} {:answer/id #uuid "e45cb0dc-146d-5654-b437-b7348a3ac476" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96002967-ff07-5fe6-945f-158c3810a07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315748} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f91d206-4154-539a-bfec-20a55e8502b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96466d8e-e8df-5a53-8c0e-feaf8be10b83" :question/math-academy-id "q-32176" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd7cc87c-1284-521d-952e-5c9a8fbd30d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315752} {:answer/id #uuid "40dfe95b-203f-5890-a4fa-bf7b97edc689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315753} {:answer/id #uuid "88e89fbd-2fea-5acc-82c8-ca6908d1f811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315754} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf40824-7877-5026-baec-79debad7d31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315755} {:answer/id #uuid "93e5fc29-8e17-5802-a80f-2bab9231120d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd7cc87c-1284-521d-952e-5c9a8fbd30d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315752} :answer-field/id #uuid "25b37808-7310-5f1e-9f58-85e367eb2209" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f9c228e-124d-5d9f-9342-052ebb13dd0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-32177" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block lower triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a69f2883-64f8-51a6-9771-d5a885809ef6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Blocks in Partitioned Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "465334f0-e00b-5eeb-b73f-f77bc2b62c0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315759} {:answer/id #uuid "786c8535-c9ec-5ab3-bba2-cc3237c4305f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315760} {:answer/id #uuid "2c5e4272-e5dd-55c0-9da9-83f0a8078d73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315761} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd84cc4-ba9b-57dd-a70e-b089327dc714" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315762} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c6d6ce-646c-5815-a142-00c14e9a4b63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7c6d6ce-646c-5815-a142-00c14e9a4b63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315763} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e7247b9-09e7-50de-8f02-deabf436c0da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6da30af-9ba3-521b-acd7-32b7ad5df3fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-42123" :question/problem "A partitioned matrix $M$ contains the following blocks: \n\n- ${M}_{11},$ which is a $2\\times 3$ block\n\n- ${M}_{12},$ which is a $2\\times 2$ block\n\n- ${M}_{22},$ which is a $1\\times 2$ block\n\nWhat are the dimensions of ${M}_{21}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have a matrix of the form\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2\\times 3 & 2\\times 2 \\\\ ?\\times ? & 1\\times 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${M}_{21}$ must be a $1\\times 3$ block."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72251ae9-36c2-5712-91c7-9e8ccae655a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315766} {:answer/id #uuid "b458c643-5d20-5413-9af2-a89fd76af9aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315767} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd31260-edb9-57b2-9574-30b7485d06f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315768} {:answer/id #uuid "cec76c25-94e5-5eda-94d8-0aed6aa599dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315769} {:answer/id #uuid "24c75603-e702-5f7a-a6f3-8b64fdd31842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cec76c25-94e5-5eda-94d8-0aed6aa599dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315769} :answer-field/id #uuid "22e65b95-9b30-549c-9c09-1658ea7ec819" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06a837c9-645b-5804-a3fa-fa0a3b0a5f81" :question/math-academy-id "q-42127" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block lower triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $B$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b507561-8134-50ff-8c23-c4ecc546450d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Determinant of a Block Diagonal or Block Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c52316-0e0d-583d-b5f4-b56fbb0a11c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315773} {:answer/id #uuid "508551e9-bf0e-543a-a743-31ab4f6440c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315774} {:answer/id #uuid "4999fda9-188f-5ca8-a794-f452ff934156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315775} {:answer/id #uuid "e80b5c44-80fc-5175-b263-46fad9f0d518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315776} {:answer/id #uuid "fe29371d-3f35-5077-8bad-dee557aec10a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e80b5c44-80fc-5175-b263-46fad9f0d518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315776} :answer-field/id #uuid "a13ff7cc-52b2-5dc5-afb1-d0622f76c3d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3312dff9-b994-52a8-a303-fbde44c8bb7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42129" :question/problem "Find \n$|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & b & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|$\ngiven that \n$|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}|=-5.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have  a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & b & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & b & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}a & 2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd27e216-162c-578f-87ff-3cce7e67e664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113842} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9790f8-b8f7-579c-8884-a0125867243d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113843} {:answer/id #uuid "d06c4efd-23ef-598e-94ae-476684f44f1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113844} {:answer/id #uuid "156463c3-0c71-5456-b9f3-abf4ea70753e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113845} {:answer/id #uuid "36ab72f9-cab4-53ba-bb85-2b86f38f98e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd27e216-162c-578f-87ff-3cce7e67e664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113842} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa414c2c-aacd-5ebe-834d-8246aa02d217" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12fdac9a-07ca-546f-8c67-8327e7b0318b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42134" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b507561-8134-50ff-8c23-c4ecc546450d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Determinant of a Block Diagonal or Block Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "989461ea-912d-55d3-8c99-96a3fca89167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315780} {:answer/id #uuid "0857d4ec-1352-5d8e-9706-75203aa174b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315781} {:answer/id #uuid "9c06e78f-84da-5214-846e-01130c389277" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315782} {:answer/id #uuid "2d939bce-797b-5889-941c-6fa5855ccf72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315783} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9ce157-b0cc-548f-975b-24511d52638b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c06e78f-84da-5214-846e-01130c389277" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315782} :answer-field/id #uuid "37aa80e8-4562-5203-93a6-ef4fe567d966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afb41d0b-8aaf-5c91-bdb1-ffd640f7baf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42139" :question/problem "Find \n$|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & d & e \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|$\ngiven that\n$|\\begin{aligned}d & e \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|=7.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a block diagonal matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & d & e \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & d & e \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}d & e \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
